{
  "title": "Tree stand: a plate held up on a trunk, loaded at three points",
  "description": "A stand 60 × 60 × 70 mm, printed as it's used: three feet close together on the bed (a trunk), a 50 mm plate on top, loaded at three points round its edge, each between two feet, plus a push sideways. 10% of the space. Each load needs its own route down, so branches should leave the trunk and split towards them; printable without supports, the 45° rule makes them rise. Attempt 1 (load over the feet) came out as a stool; attempt 2 (six loads round the edge, a twist, 15%) as a goblet: a closed cone answers a ring load and a twist.",
